invariant: INV-36
file: tools/localize_elf.zig
catches: test/localize-check.sh
reason: the ELF localizer leaves every weak definition global, so an object
  that defines one exports it. The library defines none today, which is why
  the check reads a fixture that does: llvm-objcopy -G makes first_weak local,
  and the tool's output no longer matches it.

--- old
    if (index == shn_undef) return .global;
    const kept = keep.holds(name);
--- new
    if (index == shn_undef or binding == stb_weak) return .global;
    const kept = keep.holds(name);
